 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 545760,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "A 40 in plasma television uses about 175 W. How many kilowatt-hours are needed to run the television in a month if the television is on for an average of 3 hours a day?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "15.8 kW"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{{1,000}}{{175{\\rm{\\ watts}}}} = 5.714{\\rm{\\ hours\\ to\\ use\\ 1\\ kW}}\"></span></p>\n<p>How many hours is the TV used in a month?</p>\n<p>The TV is on 3 hours per day.</p>\n<p>Use 30 days in a month as a conversion factor.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{{3{\\rm{\\ hours}}}}{{\\cancel{{{\\rm{day}}}}}}\\left( {\\frac{{30\\cancel{{{\\rm{days}}}}}}{{{\\rm{month}}}}} \\right) = 90\\frac{{{\\rm{hours}}}}{{{\\rm{month}}}}\"></span></p>\n<p>Use the knowledge that it takes about 5.714 hours to use 1 kilowatt.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"90\\frac{{{\\rm{hours}}}}{{{\\rm{month}}}}\\left( {\\frac{{1{\\rm{\\ kW}}}}{{5.714{\\rm{\\ hours}}}}} \\right) \\approx 15.8{\\rm{\\ kW}}\"></span></p>\n<p>The TV will use 15.8 kW in a month on average if it is on three hours a day.</p>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
